# Licence

This repository contains two different things under two different terms.

## The corpus — CC BY 4.0

`src/data/biases/` and the entry text rendered from it are licensed under the
Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence.

    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Reuse it, adapt it, sell things built on it. Attribute it. This is stated on
every page of the site and in `robots.txt`, and this file exists so the claim is
carried by the repository rather than only by the pages it generates.

## The code — no licence granted yet

Everything else — `build/`, `src/templates/`, `src/assets/*.js`, the workflow —
carries no licence. Under copyright law that means all rights reserved: you may
read it, and you may not redistribute or reuse it without permission.

This is a deliberate absence, not an oversight. Adding a licence is easy and
irreversible in practice, so it is left to a decision rather than a default.

## Third-party material, on its own terms

- **Fonts** in `src/assets/fonts/` are under the SIL Open Font Licence. Each
  carries its own `OFL-*.txt`, which must travel with it.
- **Icons** in `src/assets/icons/` are Tabler Icons, MIT.
- **Replication data** quoted in entries comes from FORRT's Replication Database
  (Röseler et al., *Journal of Open Psychology Data*), CC BY 4.0. Its attribution
  travels with it and appears on the pages that quote it.
- **Cited papers** are cited, not reproduced. Nothing in this repository
  redistributes a copyrighted article.
